PATCH 214: reconstruct FUN_0000_c296 (the DCBS unit-record OBJECT INITIALIZER) -- the DGROUP-near-offset
base-loss that is the ROOT of the "downstream SIGALRM-timing crash".  Asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0xc296-0xc2f1.

ROOT-CAUSE OF THE "TIMING CRASH" (proven, NOT tick re-entrancy).  With the DCBS record chain reading
correctly (patches 200/212), the installer FUN_0000_43c1 (patch 200) reaches its c296 leg:
`FUN_0000_c296((int*)di)` where di is the roster slot's DGROUP NEAR-OFFSET (e.g. 0xc05c enemy slot 0,
stride 0xfb; 0xa022 friendly).  c296 was pristine Ghidra: it treats param_1 as a HOST pointer and
derefs `*(param_1 + 0x6d)` -> wild write -> SIGSEGV.  The cascade run's `rc=139` was NONDETERMINISTIC
(rc=1 vs rc=139) ONLY because the async SIGALRM tick perturbs WHEN the process reaches this deterministic
bug; under `FIST_COOP_TICK=1` (no async tick) AND under the plain binary run through gdb (SIGALRM
passed), the crash is IDENTICAL and deterministic: `d81e -> 43c1 -> c296 (param_1=0xc05c) : *(param_1+0x6d)`.
So the documented "SIGALRM-timing crash that runs clean under gdb+COOP_TICK" is this c296 base-loss, not a
genuine tick re-entrancy -- the async timing merely masked it on some runs (survive-to-timeout).

THE FIX (faithful, same class as 43c1/8daa base-loss reconstructions 200/201/202/203).  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00,
di = the near-offset; every `[di+N]` is a DS-relative byte/word field (Ghidra also int*-scaled the
`param_1[N]`/`*param_1` forms -- e.g. asm `[di+0x90]` rendered `param_1+0x48`, a /2 scaling).  Rebuilt
from the raw asm with the explicit `g_mem+0x1c000+di` base and the real byte/word widths.  The tail
dispatches the object's per-type INIT method through the DGROUP near-vector table
word[DGROUP:(word[di]*2 - 0x1b20)]; the `call [bx-0x1b20]` keeps DI live, so di is threaded as the
callee's first arg (`typedef int code()` -> the per-type method's DI param -- the per-patch indirect
threading the doctrine prescribes).  Validated by the crash advancing strictly forward into the
dispatched method (FUN_0000_7b91 for the TANK type -- patch 215), di correctly = 0xc05c.

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (c296 is reached ONLY via the DCBS FSG parse
`4754 -> d501 -> d7e1 -> d81e -> 43c1`, which runs only on the FIST_CASCADE ACCEPT path; the 19 flows
stop at the menu/briefing and never parse a mission .FSG).  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.
Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.
